{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"ripening-liberal-tuatara","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe approved Pydantic output, bounded-operation, compatibility, and candidate-tracing children establish the replacement behavior [rebar:serge-monotonous-aruanas] [rebar:amoebaean-hemihedral-vervet]. The final change must make that path authoritative for library, CLI, MCP, plan-review, code-review, and completion operations, prove provider-cache behavior, then remove the obsolete manual retry machinery without breaking patch/import seams.\n\n## Approach\nSwitch every structured `PydanticAIRunner` consumer to the new one-operation path through the existing facade. Preserve `ProviderSession`, candidate order, output-mode policy, tool surfaces, timeout/transport limits, provenance, and serialized verdict shapes. Run the complete ticket/test oracle and authorized direct Anthropic plus Bedrock cache canaries before deletion. Once parity and approved deltas pass, remove only the obsolete structured-output attempt scheduler and temporary compatibility delegation; retain deterministic parsing, the stable runner facade, and existing public/re-export paths. Document the new retry layers, shared request budget, complete-or-omit history rule, trace-not-usage candidate semantics, and the reviewed raise-the-limit follow-up policy.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py`, `src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py`, `src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py` — authoritative call-site cutover and obsolete retry-path removal.\n- `src/rebar/llm/structured.py` — retain pure repair and stop/refusal policy; remove only dead retry integration.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/`, `src/rebar/llm/code_review/`, and completion runner consumers — compatibility verification and any narrow result projection updates.\n- `docs/llm-framework.md`, `docs/reuse-surface.md` — documented runtime and library contracts.\n- The RP-01 focused runner, structured-output, fallback, usage, failure, cache, plan-review, code-review, and completion suites.\n\n## Testing\n- Run the recovered 38-scenario behavior matrix and all focused historical ticket regressions.\n- Run lean/full import, lint, typecheck, complexity, and module-size gates.\n- Run direct Anthropic and Bedrock same-run retry canaries using environment-provided credentials without printing or persisting secrets; record cache read/write/input counts and complete-versus-omitted wire observations on the ticket.\n- Confirm rollback by temporarily selecting the pre-removal compatibility commit against the same fixtures; no stored data migration is involved.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Library, CLI, MCP, plan-review, code-review, and completion structured calls all use the one-operation Pydantic path through `PydanticAIRunner`; verified by consumer contract tests and a source reference census.\n- [ ] The recovered RP-01 behavior matrix passes with only the approved deltas: shared request exhaustion, bounded output-size retry, complete-or-omit failed response, aggregate successful-run usage, exact causal restoration, and candidate tracing outside usage.\n- [ ] No bespoke structured-output retry scheduler or fresh-Agent output-attempt loop remains; verified by source review and tests that fail if more than one outer Agent run is constructed.\n- [ ] Existing provider fallback eligibility/order, tool limits, timeout/transport ownership, provenance, final artifact policy, and serialized output shapes remain green in their historical regression suites.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Direct Anthropic and Bedrock canaries pass with secrets absent from output and artifacts; the ticket records timestamp, model ids, request counts, cache read/write/input counts, complete/omit branch, and successful typed result.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, the focused suite, module-size gate, and complexity ratchet pass with `runner.py` at or below 800 lines and every new module between 100 and 500 lines.\n- [ ] The documented retry-layer and accounting contracts match runtime behavior, including the normal plan-reviewed follow-up to raise the shared allowance if legitimate recovery is starved.","id":"10a3-7dd0-1b3d-47cc","parent_id":"905d-1287-effc-4a83","priority":2,"tags":["janitor","rp01","llm","cutover"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-01 S5 — Cut over runner consumers and remove bespoke structured-output retries"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786924779290617001,"uuid":"e56b75b4-7f81-40a6-9044-a170395dbbf9"}